    "citations": [
      {
        "id": "uk_gdpr_art_15",
        "instrument": "UK GDPR Article 15",
        "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/eur/2016/679/article/15",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
        "read": "Article 15(1) is the right to obtain confirmation whether personal data are being processed and, where that is the case, access to the personal data and the information listed in that paragraph. Article 15(1A) limits that to what the controller is able to provide based on a reasonable and proportionate search. Article 15(3) requires a copy of the personal data the data subject is entitled to under paragraph 1. Article 15(4) says the right to obtain that copy shall not adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others."
      },
      {
        "id": "dpa_sch2_para_16",
        "instrument": "Data Protection Act 2018, Schedule 2, paragraph 16",
        "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2018/12/schedule/2/paragraph/16",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
        "read": "Paragraph 16(1) says Article 15(1) to (3) do not oblige a controller to disclose information to the data subject to the extent that doing so would involve disclosing information relating to another individual who can be identified from the information. Paragraph 16(2) does not remove that obligation where the other individual has consented, or where it is reasonable to disclose without consent. Paragraph 16(3) lists circumstances the controller must have regard to. Paragraph 16(4) covers information identifying another individual as the source, and identification from other information the controller reasonably believes the data subject is likely to possess or obtain."
      },
      {
        "id": "dpa_sch2_para_18",
        "instrument": "Data Protection Act 2018, Schedule 2, paragraph 18",
        "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2018/12/schedule/2",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
        "read": "For Part 4 of Schedule 2, the listed UK GDPR provisions include Article 15(1) to (3). Paragraph 19 uses that definition."
      },
      {
        "id": "dpa_sch2_para_19",
        "instrument": "Data Protection Act 2018, Schedule 2, paragraph 19",
        "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2018/12/schedule/2/paragraph/19",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
        "read": "The listed UK GDPR provisions do not apply to personal data that consists of information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege or, in Scotland, confidentiality of communications, could be maintained in legal proceedings, or information in respect of which a duty of confidentiality is owed by a professional legal adviser to a client."
      },
      {
        "id": "ico_sar_exemptions",
        "instrument": "ICO, What exemptions are relevant for SARs?",
        "url": "https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/individual-rights/right-of-access/what-exemptions-are-relevant-for-sars/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
        "read": "The page's latest-update line says 8 December 2025. It says an exemption should be considered case by case, and that exemptions cannot be relied on routinely or applied in a blanket fashion. It also says reasons for relying on an exemption should be documented."
      },
      {
        "id": "ico_other_people",
        "instrument": "ICO, When can an exemption apply to information about other people in a SAR?",
        "url": "https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/individual-rights/right-of-access/when-can-an-exemption-apply-to-information-about-other-people-in-a-sar/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
        "read": "The page says information need not be provided in response to a SAR to the extent that this would reveal information about another person, unless that person has consented or it is reasonable to disclose without consent. It calls this the rights of others exemption, and sometimes the third-party data exemption."
      }
    ],
    "note": "The citations were read on 28 October 2026. This draft does not decide that a search was reasonable and proportionate, and it does not apply Schedule 2."
  },
